# ── Kivora security + caching headers ─────────────────────────────
# Applied by Cloudflare Pages on every response.
#
# CSP is NOT set here anymore: it is minted per-request (nonce +
# 'strict-dynamic') by middleware.js. A static CSP here would arrive as a
# SECOND policy on HTML responses — browsers enforce every CSP header
# simultaneously, so nonce'd scripts would have to satisfy both, and
# scanners would still see the legacy 'unsafe-inline'. middleware.js is
# the single source of truth for CSP (keep connect-src in sync there).
#
# This file still hardens the paths that bypass middleware (static
# assets with a file extension): /favicon.svg, /images/*, /sw.js, etc.
# NOTE: the line below overrides the platform-wide `access-control-allow-origin: *`
# that the Cloudflare Pages asset layer adds to responses (RedSentinel CORS
# finding). Nothing legitimately fetches our assets cross-origin with JS;
# <img>/<link> embeds are not CORS-gated and keep working.
# Verify after deploy: value must appear ONCE (if the platform appends
# instead of replacing, remove this line again).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://kivora.pages.dev

# Admin panel — never indexed (belt & suspenders; middleware also sets it)
/admin*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Immutable hashed assets
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
